(1.1) Math in our world Part 1
This first video presentation of Lesson 1 focuses on Patterns and Numbers  
in Nature and the World. In here, we can see that patterns in nature are  
visible regularities of form found in the natural world. These patterns  
recur in
different contexts, and interestingly, can be modeled mathematically.  
Patterns help us organize information and make sense of the world around  
us. They can be found everywhere: including in animals, plants, and even  
the solar system.
